    <!-- http://www.dfki.de/lt/onto/common/dialogue.owl#WHQuestion -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.dfki.de/lt/onto/common/dialogue.owl#WHQuestion">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.dfki.de/lt/onto/common/dialogue.owl#Question"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Communicative function of a dialogue act performed by the sender, S, in order to know which elements of a given set have a certain property specified by the semantic content; 
S puts pressure on the addressee, A, to provide this information,
which S assumes that A possesses. S believes that at least one element of the set has that property.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">originally called: &apos;Set Question&apos;</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.dfki.de/lt/onto/common/dialogue.owl#YNQuestion -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.dfki.de/lt/onto/common/dialogue.owl#YNQuestion">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.dfki.de/lt/onto/common/dialogue.owl#Question"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Communicative function of a dialogue act performed by the
sender, S, in order to know whether the proposition, which forms the semantic content, is true. 
S assumes that A knows whether the proposition is true or not, and puts pressure on A to provide this information.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">originally called: &apos;Propositional Question&apos;</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
